# XSH feraiseexcept()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Every exception macro is optional (XBD <fenv.h>): a test that uses one is
# NOTINUSE when it is not defined. Whether raising overflow or underflow also
# raises inexact is implementation-defined, so no test judges extra flags.
# No exception is ever unmasked, so no trap is taken.

assertion  XSH.feraiseexcept.001
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       feraiseexcept() returns zero for each exception the implementation
           defines.
test       t/001-return.c

assertion  XSH.feraiseexcept.002
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2001
says       After feraiseexcept() is given an exception, fetestexcept() reports
           that exception as set.
test       t/002-flag-set.c

assertion  XSH.feraiseexcept.003
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       feraiseexcept(0) returns zero and raises no exception.
test       t/003-zero.c

assertion  XSH.feraiseexcept.004
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/feraiseexcept.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       feraiseexcept(FE_ALL_EXCEPT) returns zero and every exception the
           implementation defines is set afterwards.
test       t/004-all.c
